  "notes": [
    "the record's altitude track is empty: a KML file holds tracks of positions, not an altimeter's record over time, so every value is a channel",
    "the log's zero is the first point the file times: `when` 2030-01-02T10:00:00Z",
    "4 of the file's 6 points have no time: their times are gaps",
    "`coordinates` read in meters, from the KML standard: OGC 07-147r2 states a tuple's altitude in meters, and 1 of the file's 4 tracks carry one",
    "`coordinates` kept as written, in a track whose altitude mode tells a viewer to ignore its altitude: 1 tracks, in mode clampToGround, the default, as none is stated",
    "`when` read in UTC, from the KML standard: 2 times state their zone, `Z` or an offset, as XML Schema's date-time allows"
